1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:02,927
Cent #1867.

2
00:00:06,468 --> 00:00:08,316
A penny dated 1964,

3
00:00:08,506 --> 00:00:09,589
with no mint mark,

4
00:00:09,779 --> 00:00:12,087
generally indicating the Philadelphia mint.

5
00:00:13,028 --> 00:00:14,406
Circulation leaves traces.

6
00:00:15,646 --> 00:00:17,568
In the words of Emily Watlington,

7
00:00:17,757 --> 00:00:20,425
writing on Rutherford Chang in Art in America:

8
00:00:20,615 --> 00:00:23,117
"Circulation is another of Chang's key themes:

9
00:00:23,307 --> 00:00:25,045
how do things change as they

10
00:00:25,085 --> 00:00:26,399
move through the world?"

11
00:00:27,239 --> 00:00:29,643
Rhea Myers, in her book Proof of Work,

12
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:31,681
quotes the artist Barbara Kruger:

13
00:00:31,871 --> 00:00:34,088
"Money is an information-destroying medium."

14
00:00:35,427 --> 00:00:37,838
A circulated copper cent is the exception.

15
00:00:38,277 --> 00:00:41,497
Three traits record where Cent #1867

16
00:00:41,537 --> 00:00:44,051
has been: two patinas and a contamination.

17
00:00:44,892 --> 00:00:47,393
A dark band of Significant Obsidian crosses

18
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:50,417
the upper left, over the motto and Lincoln's head.

19
00:00:51,258 --> 00:00:53,777
Green patches of Significant Verdigris gather

20
00:00:53,817 --> 00:00:56,829
on his cheek, behind his head and at his collar.

21
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:00,798
220 Cents carry Significant Obsidian,

22
00:01:00,987 --> 00:01:03,996
and 376 Significant Verdigris.

23
00:01:04,436 --> 00:01:05,629
29 carry both.

24
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:08,837
Both patinas grew from the copper.

25
00:01:09,278 --> 00:01:10,453
In the Traits Atlas,

26
00:01:10,644 --> 00:01:12,888
a patina "arises from internal chemistry".

27
00:01:13,828 --> 00:01:15,796
The third trait came from outside:

28
00:01:15,986 --> 00:01:17,652
Contaminated, Alien Secretion.

29
00:01:18,091 --> 00:01:19,739
In the Atlas, contamination

30
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,489
is "matter imposed upon copper",

31
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,896
and Alien Secretion names "unidentifiable

32
00:01:23,936 --> 00:01:25,572
translucent or greenish films".

33
00:01:26,611 --> 00:01:28,763
The Trait Council names such residues

34
00:01:28,804 --> 00:01:31,364
by reading the surface, without testing it.

35
00:01:31,804 --> 00:01:34,225
In the Atlas's words: "The subtrait names

36
00:01:34,266 --> 00:01:36,418
are therefore not claims of chemistry,

37
00:01:36,608 --> 00:01:40,506
but field names – tools for seeing." 79

38
00:01:40,546 --> 00:01:42,090
Cents carry Alien Secretion,

39
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,597
and 70 of them carry verdigris too.

40
00:01:45,638 --> 00:01:48,334
No other Cent has exactly this set of traits.

41
00:01:49,573 --> 00:01:52,730
Cent #4421 is dated the same year,

42
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,566
and is close to mint state.

43
00:01:55,006 --> 00:01:56,927
Its portrait is clean and bright.

44
00:01:57,968 --> 00:02:00,500
In March 2024, Chang inscribed

45
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:03,908
the image of Cent #1867 on a satoshi,

46
00:02:04,097 --> 00:02:05,623
and the physical coin was

47
00:02:05,664 --> 00:02:07,420
melted into CENTS Block Copper.

48
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:11,277
Released at one satoshi, the Cent's value moved

49
00:02:11,318 --> 00:02:13,222
from a figure set by the state

50
00:02:13,262 --> 00:02:14,622
into an ongoing process,

51
00:02:14,812 --> 00:02:16,430
set again each time someone

52
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:18,644
reads it, keeps it or lets it go.

53
00:02:20,084 --> 00:02:22,782
Cent #1867, a great Cent.
